# Permissions & Auth

## Permission naming
Format: `{module}.{action}` — e.g. `income.create`, `users.changepassword`

Modules: `accounts`, `income`, `cost`, `users`, `persons`, `persongroups`, `costtypes`, `food`, `reports`, `deathanniversaries`, `generaltypes`, `attachments`, `audit`, `messages`, `messagechannels`

Standard actions: `view`, `create`, `update`, `delete` (+ `users.changepassword`, `attachments.add`)

`messages` — menu **مرکز پیام** (پیکربندی): `view` = list log, `send` = compose + income receipt + death-anniversary channel notify + sync-contacts / register-webhooks (UI under **تنظیمات → پیام‌رسان‌ها**), `update` = edit on channel (within 48h; not person-group broadcasts), `delete` = remote (`scope=remote`) or local (`scope=local`)

`deathanniversaries` — menu **سالگرد وفات**: `view` = report; with `messages.send`, `POST /api/reports/death-anniversaries/notify` sends Text or Photo (condolence card) per person to selected message channels

Which messengers appear in Message Center compose and income receipt: device preference in Settings (`uiPrefs.enabledMessengers` / localStorage). Toggle is enabled only when that bot token is configured on the server (`GET /api/messages/config` → `isConfigured`); otherwise Settings shows setup steps for the env/appsettings keys.

`messagechannels` — menu **کانال‌های پیام** (پیکربندی): CRUD named channels (`MessengerKind` + `ExternalChatId` string — Bale/Telegram: numeric/`@username`; Rubika: opaque chat_id)

`persongroups` — menu **گروه‌های اشخاص** (اطلاعات پایه): CRUD named person groups for broadcast compose

Bale contact linking: mobile on Person → webhook `POST /api/bale/webhook` or `sync-contacts` → `BaleContactLink` + `Person.BaleChatId` (read-only in API). `BaleBotState.LastUpdateId` dedupes webhook/poll updates; first `getUpdates` uses `offset=-1` to skip backlog. Person-group sends may sit in `AwaitingContact` until linked.

Rubika contact linking: mobile on Person → webhook `POST /api/rubika/webhook` (`{ update }`) or same `sync-contacts` → `RubikaContactLink` + `Person.RubikaChatId`. Contact request via ChatKeypad `AskMyPhoneNumber`. `RubikaBotState.LastOffsetId` stores `next_offset_id`; first poll stores offset without linking backlog.

Telegram contact linking: mobile on Person → webhook `POST /api/telegram/webhook` (header `X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token` when configured) or same `sync-contacts` → `TelegramContactLink` + `Person.TelegramChatId`. Same `/start` + share-phone flow as Bale (`https://t.me/{bot}?start=person_{id}`). `TelegramBotState.LastUpdateId` dedupes updates.

WhatsApp Cloud API: `WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN` + `WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID`; phone-first `wa_id` from Person.Mobile → `Person.WhatsAppChatId` / `WhatsAppContactLink`. Webhook `GET/POST /api/whatsapp/webhook` (verify token + optional app secret). No remote edit/delete. Meta may require templates outside the 24h customer-care window.

Messenger extensibility: `IMessengerSender` + `MessengerKind` (`Bale`, `Rubika`, `Telegram`, `WhatsApp`); remote message ids stored as strings on `MessengerMessage` for all messengers; channels are per-messenger; HTTP surface `/api/messages` with multi-messenger compose (`Messengers[]`).

`attachments` has no menu — `view` = list/preview, `add` = upload, `delete` = remove saved file

`audit` has no menu — `view` = on-demand created/updated metadata panel (stripped from API without permission)

## Source of truth
- Backend: `PermissionCodes.cs` — `All` array drives DB seed
- JWT claims: `"permission"` claim per granted code
- Frontend: permissions array on login/profile; cached in localStorage

## Backend enforcement
```csharp
[RequirePermission(PermissionCodes.FoodUpdate)]
```
`PermissionFilter` — unauthenticated → 401; missing permission → 403

## Frontend enforcement
- Route guard: `meta.permission` or `meta.permissionsAny`; denied → `resolveHomePath()` (no empty dashboard)
- `/` redirects to first accessible **operational** module (income → cost → … → reports → more)
- Sidebar / More menu groups: **عملیات** → **اطلاعات پایه** (اشخاص، حساب‌ها، …) → **پیکربندی** → **گزارشات**
- Mobile bottom tabs: درآمد · هزینه · گزارشات · **بیشتر** (overflow at the end, never middle)
- Income/cost/food menu + route: visible with `*.view` **or** `*.create` **or** `*.update`
- Without `*.view`, list/update/delete are limited to records created by the current user
- UI: hide buttons/rows with `auth.hasPermission`
- Never rely on UI alone — API must always enforce

## User permissions editor
- Component: `PermissionMatrix.vue` + `usePermissionMatrix.js`
- Grouped by module; desktop horizontal checkboxes in 2-col cards; mobile vertical tappable rows
- Persisted with user create/update — same permission codes as JWT claims
- Transaction forms use `/api/lookups/*`; admin `accounts.view` / `costtypes.view` not required for income/cost create
- PersonSelect search: `GET /api/lookups/persons` (persons.view/create/update **or** income.view/create/update)

## Special cases
- `users.changepassword` — separate from `users.update`; dedicated `PUT /api/users/{id}/password`
- System admin (`admin`) — cannot edit/delete from users page; password/avatar only via profile
- New permissions auto-added to DB on startup; assigned to admin only (not all users)
